          "items": [
            {
              "id": "text-47",
              "kind": "text",
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "heading",
                  "level": 2,
                  "text": "Military Aircraft | Engines"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Stringent requirements in military aircraft engines make Titanium an excellent material of choice. Due to Titanium’s high strength-to-weight ratio, ability to withstand high temperatures and corrosion resistances make this metal perfect for aircraft engine applications. Titanium is the most common material of choice for engine parts that operate at temperatures up to 1100 degrees F or 593 degrees C."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Titanium components designed in an military aircraft engine include blades, disc, hubs, inlet guide vanes and cases."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "row-48",
      "preset": "wide-fifths",
      "spaceAbove": false,
      "columns": [
        {
          "id": "column-49",
          "items": [
            {
              "id": "text-51",
              "kind": "text",
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "heading",
                  "level": 2,
                  "text": "Military Rotorcraft"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Titanium can be found in both military and commercial helicopters applications that include exhaust ducts, wind access panels, landing gear, brackets, rotors and blades, and many other areas."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The UH-60 Black Hawk helicopter, as an example, contains a four-bladed primary rotor and one four-bladed tail rotor that are built with Titanium cores. Because of this use, the rotors are mostly resistant against anti-aircraft artillery fire up to 23mm."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "column-50",
          "items": [
            {
              "id": "picture-52",
              "kind": "picture",
              "src": "https://titanium.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/military-2.jpg",
              "alt": "military-2",
              "href": "",
              "wrap": "none"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "row-53",
      "preset": "quality-split",
      "spaceAbove": false,
      "columns": [
        {
          "id": "column-54",
          "items": [
            {
              "id": "picture-56",
              "kind": "picture",
              "src": "https://titanium.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/military-1.jpg",
              "alt": "Defense | Specialty Metals | Markets | Titanium Industries",
              "href": "",
              "wrap": "none"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "column-55",
          "items": [
            {
              "id": "text-57",
              "kind": "text",
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "heading",
                  "level": 2,
                  "text": "Land & Combat Vehicles"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Military land and combat vehicles have also seen Titanium usage increase over the last 2 decades and is primarily used due to Titanium’s low weight-to-strength ratio, excellent mechanical and ballistic properties, and ease of fabrication. These applications generally focus around armor plating and non-structural components to reduce vehicle weight, better overall performance, and allow for other upgrades. The most common Titanium grades used are 6Al-4V Grade 5 and 6Al-4V ELI Grade 23 with 6Al-6v-2Sn primarily being used for ordinance components and frames."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "row-58",
      "preset": "wide-fifths",
      "spaceAbove": false,
      "columns": [
        {
          "id": "column-59",
          "items": [
            {
              "id": "text-61",
              "kind": "text",
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "heading",
                  "level": 2,
                  "text": "Naval & Marine"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Titanium’s excellent corrosion resistance, high strength-to-weight ratio, fatigue resistance, and defense against pitting makes it a preferred material in naval applications. Applications like propeller shafts, underwater robotics, rigging equipment, ball valves, marine heat exchangers, piping, onboard cooling systems, fire system piping and pumps, exhaust stack liners, and many others have become ideal candidates for Titanium."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Prior to the use of Titanium, damage to these essential components and systems was frequent. Repair and replacements were so often that Titanium was introduced to significantly increase and improve material lifespan and reduce service costs."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "To gain further insights into Titanium Industries and the diverse markets we cater to with our specialty metals, we invite you to explore our range of other markets:"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "[Aerospace](https://titanium.com/markets/aerospace/) [Industrial](https://titanium.com/markets/industrial/) [Medical](https://titanium.com/markets/medical/) [Defense](https://titanium.com/markets/defense/) [Engineered Fastener Alloys](https://titanium.com/markets/engineered-fasteners/) [Consumer Products](https://titanium.com/markets/consumer-products/) [Interconnect](https://titanium.com/interconnect-alloys/) [Additive Manufacturing](https://titanium.com/markets/additive_manufacturing/)"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Follow us on Social Media:"
                }
              ]
            },
